{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A vertex is discovered, then its out-edges are reported, then it is finished. An edge to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undiscovered vertex is a tree edge, and the search continues from that vertex before the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge. An edge to a vertex discovered but not yet finished is a back edge; a self-loop is one.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An edge to a finished vertex is a forward edge when that vertex was discovered later than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"vertex being explored, and a cross edge otherwise.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a directed graph every out-edge of an explored vertex is reported. In an undirected graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each edge is reported once, from the end that reaches it first: the tree edge is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported again from the vertex it discovered, but a parallel edge to the parent is a back edge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a self-loop is one back edge. Without pruning or a depth limit an undirected search has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only tree and back edges; an edge to a finished vertex whose edges were not explored is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forward or cross edge.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What an edge depth-first search reports, in order: the events of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each edge given by its position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", so parallel edges are told apart."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearchevent"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"}],"title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","externalID":"s:9Traversal25EdgeDepthFirstSearchEventO","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"symbolKind":"enum","remoteSource":{"fileName":"EdgeSearchEvents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/EdgeSearchEvents.swift#L37"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/backEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/docume